 {:seon.task/name "seon-runs-on-linux-in-a-container"
  :seon.task/plan "Not ready: waits on the Jolt pins it lists (jolt.process, jolt.io-poller, jolt.async Linux tasks) and seon.agent/the-agent-is-a-flow-graph; the Deep fixes session owns the Jolt side. The owner, 2026-10-30: native macOS and a Docker option is pretty good reach for now. Seon builds and runs on a Linux host, shown by an arm64 Linux container on this Mac (Docker Desktop, 29.9, 10 CPUs, 16 GB): one bin/ way to build Seon in the container (Chez, Jolt, the native libs, target/seon), run bin/prove there, and start a root with an agent working a task. Needs first: the Jolt pin of jolt.process/a-childs-exit-is-a-channel-value, jolt.process/the-hosts-memory-and-signals-are-jolts, jolt.io-poller/wake-on-signals-on-linux, jolt.async/a-forked-child-closes-inherited-ends-on-linux and jolt.async/a-remote-end-carries-descriptors (the platform differences in Jolt, behind one interface: the owner, 2026-10-30), and seon.agent/the-agent-is-a-flow-graph (one agent loop, the lib/macos? gate gone). The Jolt gates' run in the container is its first user. Done: in the container, bin/build, bin/prove OK, and an e2e calc green, each command named in docs/machine.md; what differs from macOS (memory as Linux charges it, signals) said there."
